From: Tabor SPE port maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] debian/control: take libnss-myhostname for the build architecture

libnss-myhostname is a build dependency so the build can always resolve
its hostname (Debian #1063648). The NSS module is loaded by the build
tools' libc, which in a cross build is the build architecture's, so
qualify it :native. A cross build otherwise needs libnss-myhostname for
the host architecture, which is only built with systemd. Native builds
are unchanged.
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
                libkeyutils-dev [linux-any],
                libldap2-dev <!stage1>,
                liblmdb-dev, 
-               libnss-myhostname, 
+               libnss-myhostname:native, 
                libsasl2-dev <!stage1>,
                libssl-dev,
                libverto-dev,
